course: dictionary
lesson: 11328
title: Yogurt and helpful bacteria
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Yogurt is a thick, slightly sour food made from milk. Special helpful bacteria are added to the milk, and they change it over time. «Bacteria turn milk into yogurt and cheese.» Without the bacteria, you would only have milk.
explain: Read the words around yogurt to work out what it means. «I had a strawberry yogurt» tells you that a yogurt can be a small pot of food that you eat for breakfast or in your lunchbox. Yogurt can be plain, Greek or frozen, and each one is still yogurt.
explain: Bacteria have a bad name, but most of them are harmless or helpful. «Most bacteria are harmless or helpful: they rot dead things, help us digest food and turn milk into yogurt; only a few cause illness.» The sentence tells you which bacteria are the useful ones. Yeast is different: it makes bread rise by giving off bubbles of gas.
fact: Yogurt is a thick, slightly sour food made from milk.
fact: Helpful bacteria are added to milk to make yogurt.
fact: «Bacteria turn milk into yogurt and cheese.»
fact: Most bacteria are harmless or helpful; only a few cause illness.
fact: A pot of yogurt is one small container of this food.
exercise: «Bacteria turn milk into yogurt and cheese.» What do the bacteria do to the milk? | Freeze it solid | *Turn it into yogurt and cheese | Pour it into a bottle | Add sugar to it
exercise: «I had a strawberry yogurt.» What is a yogurt here? | A glass of milk | *A small pot of this food | A spoon for eating | A kind of strawberry
exercise: Ella says all bacteria make people ill. Is she right? | Yes, only the bacteria in milk are ill | Yes, every bacterium makes you ill | No, bacteria are not real | *No, most bacteria are harmless or helpful
test: What does «plain yogurt» tell you about the yogurt? | It is made from fruit | It comes in a bottle | *It has no fruit or sweet flavour added | It is always frozen
test: What do the helpful bacteria do in yogurt? | They freeze milk into ice | They turn yogurt into water | *They turn milk into yogurt | They make bubbles of gas in bread
exam: A shop sells pots of yogurt, 3 pots for £2. How much do 6 pots cost? | *£4 | £6 | £2 | £12
